---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="AI Ecommerce for Smarter Shopping and Operations | Kelp"
  description="Use AI in ecommerce to improve product discovery, catalog work, customer help, and connected operations without losing control of product facts."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="AI Services"
    title="AI Ecommerce Built on Product Data You Can Trust"
    description="AI can help shoppers find a better fit and help teams manage a complicated catalog. It cannot fix a wrong price, missing specification, or inventory system that disagrees with the store. Kelp brings AI Ecommerce into the storefront and the operations behind it, starting with the information each experience needs."
    lottieFile="ai-ecommerce.json"
  />
  <section class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where Teams Get Stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Merchants are being offered AI product descriptions, shopping
        assistants, and merchandising tools from every direction. The hard part
        is deciding which one solves a real problem. A recommendation is only
        useful if it understands variants and compatibility. An answer about
        availability needs current stock. A generated description still needs
        verified product facts and a voice that sounds like the brand.
      </p>
      <h2>How We Fix It</h2>
      <p>
        We map the customer decision and the product data that supports it. Then
        we choose a focused application for AI, design the experience, and
        connect it to the right sources. Catalog structure, storefront
        usability, inventory, and fulfillment remain part of the plan because a
        helpful AI interaction still has to lead to a valid order.
      </p>
      <h2>Make the Catalog Easier to Understand</h2>
      <p>
        Titles, attributes, variants, images, compatibility, and policies need a
        consistent home. We can help organize the data and the workflow for
        maintaining it. AI may speed up drafting or categorization, while staff
        verify claims and keep the source information current. That work also
        improves ordinary search, filters, and product pages.
      </p>
      <h2>Help Shoppers Choose</h2>
      <p>
        A guided assistant or product comparison can answer practical questions,
        narrow options, and point people to the right item. For custom products,
        it may need to understand configuration rules and collect details the
        production team can use. We design the path through product selection,
        cart, and checkout rather than treating the AI exchange as a separate
        experience.
      </p>
      <h2>Connect Discovery to the Order</h2>
      <p>
        Kelp's <a href="/services/ecommerce/">ecommerce development work</a>{" "}
        covers Shopify, WooCommerce, custom products, and connections to POS,
        ERP, inventory, shipping, and production systems. We can scope how an AI
        experience uses that information, what it is allowed to say or do, and
        how the team checks outcomes.{" "}
        <a href="/platforms/shopify/">Our Shopify work</a> can support the
        storefront side of the experience.
      </p>
      <h2>Measure the Result That Matters</h2>
      <p>
        We look beyond whether shoppers clicked an AI feature. Did they find a
        suitable product, complete an order, reduce avoidable support questions,
        or create fewer fulfillment exceptions? We use those signals to decide
        whether the experience deserves a wider rollout. AI shopping visibility
        can change, and no agency can promise a product will be recommended by a
        third-party answer system.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Product-data and customer-journey review</li>
        <li>AI use-case and storefront experience design</li>
        <li>Catalog, assistant, or workflow implementation</li>
        <li>Connections to commerce and operations systems</li>
        <li>Quality checks and measurement of real outcomes</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        Bring a product category that customers struggle to shop or that staff
        struggle to maintain. We can look at the data, storefront, and order
        workflow together, then recommend where AI Ecommerce would genuinely
        help. Talk with Kelp about the store.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3 class="h4">Do we need to rebuild our store to use AI Ecommerce?</h3>
      <p>
        Not always. We review the current platform, product data, and
        integrations first. A focused improvement may work within the existing
        store; a broader rebuild makes sense when the underlying system blocks
        the experience you need.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Talk Through Your Project
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
